{"resource": {"name": "Berkeley PD - Stop Data (October 1, 2020 - Present)", "id": "ysvs-bcge", "parent_fxf": [], "description": "Berkeley PD transitioned to RIPA stop data collection effective October 1, 2020.  Data collected from these stops conforms to requirements set forth in Government Code section 12525.5 that was enacted as a result of AB 953, the Racial and Identity Profiling Act (RIPA) of 2015 (https://oag.ca.gov/ab953).  Berkeley PD will begin reporting RIPA data to the CA DOJ effective January 1, 2021.\n\nFor more information about any of the column definitions, please download the document:  One Page Narrative for Stop Data (October 1, 2020).pdf.", "attribution": "City of Berkeley Police Department", "attribution_link": null, "contact_email": null, "type": "dataset", "updatedAt": "2022-12-14T21:01:59.000Z", "createdAt": "2020-12-03T23:16:16.000Z", "metadata_updated_at": "2022-12-14T21:01:52.000Z", "data_updated_at": "2022-12-14T21:01:59.000Z", "columns_name": ["Person Number", "Time of Stop", "Basis for Search", "Result of Stop", "Type Of Stop", "Perceived Gender", "Officer Type of Assignment", "School Name", "Education Code Section", "Perceived or Known Disability", "Reason for Stop", "LAT", "Date of Stop", "Citation Offense Codes", "Actions Taken", "Information Based Stop", "City", "Is Location a K12 Public School", "Education Code Subdivision", "Is Stop Made in Response to Call for Service", "Is LGBT", "Contraband or Evidence", "Perceived Gender Nonconforming", "LONG", "Custodial arrest Offense Codes", "In field cite and release Offense Codes", "Warning Offense Codes", "Other Contraband Desc", "Location", "Duration of Stop", "LEA Record ID", "Type of Property Seized", "Basis for Property Seizure", "City of Residence", "Perceived Age", "If K12 School Is Stop of a Student", "Basis for Search Narrative", "Suspicion Offense Code", "Traffic Violation Offense Codes", "Traffic Violation Type", "Suspicion SubType", "Race Perceived Prior To Stop", "Reason for